  <section id="spot" class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="spot-heading">
    <h2 id="spot-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Spot API</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Spot V3 is a separate API on <code>{ASTER_API_FACTS.spotRestBase}</code> with endpoints under{" "}
      <code>/api/v3/*</code> and a WebSocket at <code>{ASTER_API_FACTS.spotWsBase}</code>. The live spot exchangeInfo
      listed 79 symbols. Spot rate limits are higher than futures, but FOK is not supported for spot order placement.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[#1e293b]/60">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-brand-950/60 border-b border-[#1e293b]/40">
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Method</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Path</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Auth</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Note</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {spotEndpoints.map((endpoint) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-[#1e293b]/30 last:border-b-0">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-300 font-mono">{endpoint.method}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-sky-300 font-mono whitespace-nowrap">{endpoint.path}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">{endpoint.purpose}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">{endpoint.auth}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">{endpoint.note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Spot depth weight is 2 for limits 5–50, 5 for 100, 10 for 500 and 20 for 1,000. Klines allow up to 1,500 points.
      <code>historicalTrades</code> and <code>commissionRate</code> require a signed request.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="websocket" class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="ws-heading">
    <h2 id="ws-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">WebSocket streams</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Futures stream from <code>{ASTER_API_FACTS.wsBase}</code>; spot streams from{" "}
      <code>{ASTER_API_FACTS.spotWsBase}</code>. Stream names and symbols must be lowercase. Combined streams wrap each
      event as <code>{`{"stream":"...","data":{...}}`}</code>.
    </p>
    <pre class="bg-brand-950/70 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 overflow-x-auto"><code class="text-xs text-sky-200">{`{
  "method": "SUBSCRIBE",
  "params": ["btcusdt@aggTrade", "btcusdt@bookTicker"],
  "id": 1
}`}</code></pre>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[#1e293b]/60">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-brand-950/60 border-b border-[#1e293b]/40">
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Surface</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Stream</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Payload</th>
            <th scope="col" class="text-left text-[10px] text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-widest px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Update</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {[...futuresStreams, ...spotStreams].map((stream) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-[#1e293b]/30 last:border-b-0">
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-300 font-mono">{stream.surface}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-sky-300 font-mono">{stream.name}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">{stream.payload}</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-400">{stream.speed}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
      <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">bookTicker payload</h3>
      <pre class="bg-brand-950/70 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-lg p-4 overflow-x-auto"><code class="text-xs text-sky-200">{`{
  "e": "bookTicker",
  "u": 400900217,
  "s": "BTCUSDT",
  "b": "25.35190000",  // best bid price
  "B": "31.21000000",  // best bid qty
  "a": "25.36520000",  // best ask price
  "A": "40.66000000"   // best ask qty
}`}</code></pre>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
        For order and position updates, open a user data stream with a listen key and keep it alive. Futures allows 10
        inbound messages per second; spot allows 5.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

