  <section id="data-providers" class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="providers-heading">
    <h2 id="providers-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Official API vs indexed data</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      The official API is for trading and account state. Indexed providers decode on-chain events for analytics and
      backfills. They solve different jobs and should not be confused.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Official Aster API</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Orders, positions, balances, funding and user data streams.</li>
          <li>Auth via V1 HMAC or V3 API Wallet.</li>
          <li>Real-time exchange state, not historical analytics.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">Indexed data providers</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          <li>Decoded trades, funding settlements, liquidations and order fills.</li>
          <li>GraphQL for history, WebSocket for streams, Kafka for pipelines.</li>
          <li>Useful for backtesting, dashboards and cross-venue analytics.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      {ASTER_DATA_PROVIDERS.map((provider) => (
        <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">{provider.name}</h3>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">{provider.type}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{provider.description}</p>
          <a href={provider.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[11px] font-mono text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">
            Aster DEX data product ↗
          </a>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="changelog" class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="changelog-heading">
    <h2 id="changelog-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Changelog watch</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      The official CHANGELOG is the source for breaking changes. These are the entries most likely to affect an
      integration:
    </p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      {ASTER_API_CHANGES.map((entry) => (
        <li><strong class="text-slate-300">{entry.date}:</strong> {entry.change}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Full history: <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.changelog} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Aster API CHANGELOG</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="sdk" class="space-y-3 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="sdk-heading">
    <h2 id="sdk-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">SDK and GitHub</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-slate-200">No verified official Python package was found at the time of writing.</strong> The
      legacy guide referenced <code>aster-connector-python</code> with a <code>Frenchie</code> client; that package does
      not resolve on PyPI or GitHub, so the import example is not safe to reuse.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      The official reference includes Python EIP-712 signing examples. The AgentSkills repository is the closest official
      integration layer. Start there:
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.docs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">futures V3</a>
      {" · "}
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.spotDocs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">spot V3</a>
      {" · "}
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">api-docs repository</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="bot" class="space-y-3 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="bot-heading">
    <h2 id="bot-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Trading bot checklist</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li>One key and one API Wallet per strategy; separate permissions.</li>
        <li>Bind the key to the bot's egress IP.</li>
        <li>Store secrets in a secret manager, never in the repository or logs.</li>
        <li>Generate microsecond nonces carefully; do not reuse them across agents.</li>
        <li>Use <code>recvWindow</code> ≤ 5,000 ms and handle nonce rejections.</li>
      </ul>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
        <li>Subscribe to the user data stream for order and position state.</li>
        <li>Budget request weight; cache <code>exchangeInfo</code> and refresh it deliberately.</li>
        <li>On 503, query before retrying; on 418, stop.</li>
        <li>Use testnet for first deployment and separate hosts for futures and spot.</li>
        <li>Implement a kill switch that cancels orders and flattens positions.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="space-y-4 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
    <h2 id="faq-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      {ASTER_API_FAQ.map((item) => (
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100">{item.question}</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{item.answer}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-3">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Sources: <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.apiPage} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Aster API overview</a> ·
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.docs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">futures V3 reference</a> ·
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.spotDocs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">spot V3 reference</a> ·
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.rpcDocs} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Chain RPC</a> ·
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.changelog} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">changelog</a> ·
      <a href={ASTER_API_FACTS.skillsHub} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">skills hub</a> ·
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}resources/terms-and-conditions`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Terms of service</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> · Published by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
